message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Loops cannot see most registration error: measuring the visibility ceiling of cycle consistency"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "draft methods note"
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://parallaxmetrology.com/loop-visibility/
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/loop-visibility
keywords: [image registration, deformable registration, cycle consistency, transitivity, inverse consistency, quality assurance, Hodge decomposition, DIR-Lab, 4DCT, radiotherapy]
abstract: >
  The part of a set of pairwise registrations that fails to close around loops is exactly the part of its
  error that fails to close, because true displacements are differences of positions. Splitting the error on
  the registration graph into integrable and cyclic parts gives the share any closure-based check can see.
  On DIR-Lab thoracic 4DCT, 93.1% of whole-volume Demons error and 79.1% of a local translation registrar's
  error is invisible to every loop, against 33.3% if errors were independent.
